  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA, single-profile, PCA n2000) achieved 0.485 acc, while config_010 (image, ResNet50) was very weak at 0.208 acc, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. The key uncertainty is whether a learned RNA encoder (scvi) can substantially outperform the PCA baseline, since the encoder choice is a fundamental design axis that propagates to all multiprofile and multimodal configurations. This experiment (config_004: RNA-only, single-profile, scvi_n200) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_001, isolating the encoder effect. If scvi improves meaningfully over PCA, it justifies prioritizing scvi-based multiprofile and multimodal configs in the remaining 7 experiments; if it does not, PCA remains the preferred encoder and budget can focus on profile/aggregation/fusion. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice given the sparse evidence."
}

